{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/JPEG Signature.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/JPEG Signature.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"jpeg signature jpeg signature","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/JPEG Signature.md","fileName":"JPEG Signature.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"JPEG Signature","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-16 00:47\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Image Metadata and JPEG Signatures]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Image Metadata and JPEG Signatures","fakephotos.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/JPEG Signature.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/JPEG Signature.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"jpeg signature jpeg signature","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/JPEG Signature.md","fileName":"JPEG Signature.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"JPEG Signature","heading":"JPEG Signature","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A JPEG signature is a collection of encoding choices that can characterize a camera or software pipeline. Quantization tables, embedded-thumbnail properties, and the order and contents of marker segments are particularly useful because different devices and applications package JPEG data differently.\n\nA mismatch between a file's signature and its claimed source suggests that the image was resaved or did not come directly from that pipeline. A match is not proof of origin, since signatures can be shared, copied, or changed by firmware and export settings.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Image Metadata and JPEG Signatures","fakephotos.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/JPEG Signature.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/JPEG Signature.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"jpeg signature jpeg signature","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/JPEG